 "result": "The default session is a signed-cookie session. `SignedCookieSessionInterface` in `src/tessel/sessions.py` sets its `serializer` to `session_json_serializer`, which is a `TypedCookieSerializer` instance. The serializer lives in `src/tessel/json/tag.py`.\n\n- **Tags:** `TypedCookieSerializer` has a tag for each special type: tuple, bytes, Markup, UUID, datetime, and dicts containing a `\" di\"` key. On save, each value is wrapped in its tag so it can be written as plain JSON. On load, the tag tells the serializer which type to rebuild.\n- **Signing:** `SignedCookieSessionInterface.make_signer(app)` builds an itsdangerous `URLSafeTimedSerializer` that wraps this serializer to sign the payload.\n- **Session object:** `SignedCookieSession` (a `CallbackDict` plus `SessionMixin`) holds the data in memory.\n- **Save and load:** `persist_session` and `restore_session` on the interface do the encoding and decoding.\n\nI took this from `brain/sessions.md` and didn't open the source files, so the individual tag class names inside `tag.py` aren't confirmed.",
